a of the pentagon in terms of x and", "x0": 0.17692307692307693, "y0": 0.5516705516705517, "x1": 0.8087912087912088, "y1": 0.5648795648795649}, {"text": "trigonometric ratios.", "x0": 0.22747252747252747, "y0": 0.5687645687645687, "x1": 0.3901098901098901, "y1": 0.581973581973582}, {"text": "(b) The population P of a city is growing at a rate that is proportional to the current 4", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6153846153846154, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.6348096348096348}, {"text": "population. The population at time \u00a2 years is given by", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.6317016317016317, "x1": 0.6, "y1": 0.6511266511266511}, {"text": "where A and k are constants.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.7024087024087025, "x1": 0.3967032967032967, "y1": 0.7125097125097125}, {"text": "The population at time 0 was 1 000 000 and at time t= 2 was 1 072 500.", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.7350427350427351, "x1": 0.7934065934065934, "y1": 0.7482517482517482}, {"text": "(i) Find the value of A.", "x0": 0.18681318681318682, "y0": 0.7692307692307693, "x1": 0.38571428571428573, "y1": 0.7816627816627817}, {"text": "(ii) Find the value of k.", "x0": 0.1813186813186813, "y0": 0.8026418026418026, "x1": 0.3824175824175824, "y1": 0.815073815073815}, {"text": "(iii) At what time will the population reach 2 000 000?", "x0": 0.17582417582417584, "y0": 0.8352758352758353, "x1": 0.634065934065934, "y1": 0.8484848484848485}], [{"text": "QUESTION 6. Use a SEPARATE Writing Booklet. Marks", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.08391608391608392, "x1": 0.8802197802197802, "y1": 0.09712509712509712}, {"text": "(a) A particle P moves along a straight line for 8 seconds, starting at the fixed 5", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.13053613053613053, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.14996114996114995}, {"text": "point S at time t = 0. At time \u00a2 seconds, P is x(t) metres to the right of S. The", "x0": 0.16703296703296702, "y0": 0.15073815073815075, "x1": 0.80879120879120